b:
The minute you learn that [Person A] was a pageant girl, you will understand. The whole girly drama, behind-the-back talking, and idea that she *must* get along with everyone (even if its fake and surface level) is ingrained in her blood.

&amp;#x200B;

She just cannot wrap her head around the fact that [Person B] is a tomboy type and doesn't subscribe to [Person A]'s way of life and friendship. [Person B] just wants to have fun, workout, and be silly. [Person A] wants her to huddle around the beanbags and stir drama. You couldn't have found two girls who are further apart.

&amp;#x200B;

THE ONLY PROBLEM here is that when [Person B] seems to get the fact that they are different, but [Person A] doesn't accept who she is and is trying to change her to become someone like her. Everything we have seen is [Person A] bullying and manipulating [Person B] to change her actions and behaviors. Why should anyone change who they are to please you? [Person B] during all of this has never insulted or done [Person A] wrong. This whole situation has been started and continued by [Person A] because [Person B] chooses to spend time with other people.

She 100% deserves it. One of the most immature and fake contestants on the show.

&amp;#x200B;

She sees one person chatting with another. "Oh, Im going to sit on his lap and be affectionate for 3min and then come back guys." to two others. What a fake calculated human being.

&amp;#x200B;

Imagine needing to say that about any other real couple. She is just not a good person and has no real love for her partner. Literally using him as an object and her ticket to stay in the villa.

I wouldn't ever be that rude even arguing with the spouse, let alone someone who I have only known for two weeks. She is acting way out of hand. There is no realistic context on a dating show where that is acceptable.

&nbsp;

Just look at how mature and calm the two participants were.
